<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
        nexus-ndoke — nx_answer_steps gains the two cache-token columns whose
        values the client ALREADY PARSES and then discards.

        WHAT IS BROKEN WITHOUT THIS. The Anthropic usage envelope reports CACHED
        input separately from fresh input. A cached prompt reports
        input_tokens=2 with the real size in cache_creation_input_tokens (cold)
        or cache_read_input_tokens (warm). Measured directly on two dispatch
        envelopes:
            cold: input_tokens=2, cache_creation_input_tokens=26068, cache_read=0
            warm: input_tokens=2, cache_read_input_tokens=16324
        telemetry-007 stores only input_tokens / output_tokens / cost_usd, so
        input_tokens reads 2 on essentially every recorded step against
        1,500-5,000 output tokens. It is not the prompt size and cannot be used
        as one.

        CONSEQUENCE, and why this is a correctness bug rather than a missing
        nice-to-have: every per-plan cost aggregate computed from these rows is
        a MIXTURE of cache-warm and cache-cold runs with nothing recorded that
        can separate them. RDR-196's own numbers are affected. Found by joining
        nx_answer_steps to the 17 recorded runs of the plan=357 shakedown probe:
        the 0.8851 run and the 0.0843 run share the same model and their output
        tokens differ by ONE (1685 vs 1684), yet cost differs 10x. Model tiering
        was REFUTED as the explanation — every run in both humps is
        claude-opus-5. Cache hit vs miss is the mechanism, and it is the one
        dimension the table cannot express.

        THIS IS PLUMBING, NOT NEW INSTRUMENTATION. nexus.operators.dispatch's
        DispatchUsage already carries cache_read_input_tokens and
        cache_creation_input_tokens, populated from the stream-json result
        event. The values are captured and then dropped at the persistence
        boundary because there was nowhere to put them.

        NULLABLE, mirroring telemetry-007's own reasoning for input_tokens /
        output_tokens / cost_usd: a step whose envelope carried no usage must
        record ABSENCE, not 0. A stored 0 reads as "this call used no cached
        input", which is a measurement claim the run never made — the same
        distinction telemetry-007-3 made when it dropped cost_usd's NOT NULL and
        DEFAULT 0.0. Rows written before this changeset stay NULL and are
        correctly unattributable rather than silently reading as cache-cold.

        INTEGER to match input_tokens / output_tokens exactly; these are counts
        from the same envelope and there is no reason for them to diverge in
        type from their siblings.
    -->

    <changeSet id="telemetry-008-1" author="nexus-ndoke">
        <comment>nx_answer_steps: add cache_read_input_tokens + cache_creation_input_tokens (nullable, mirroring the sibling token columns)</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS cache_read_input_tokens INTEGER;
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS cache_creation_input_tokens INTEGER;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS cache_creation_input_tokens;
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS cache_read_input_tokens;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
